            <ArticleTitle>Early stent occlusion is not always caused by thrombosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Early occlusion of intracoronary stents has been exclusively attributed to thrombosis. Using intracoronary angioscopy, we have found 2 patients in whom this common and serious complication of coronary stenting was caused by obstructive intima dissection rather than thrombosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
